  "id": "Compound::DB00853 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Temozolomide is linked to Cyp3a4 through a shared pathway in the Alkylating Activity category, which includes compounds like Lomustine, Trabectedin, and Ifosfamide. These compounds all bind to Cyp3a4, suggesting a common mechanism of interaction with the cytochrome P450 3A4 enzyme. The lowest common ancestors of Temozolomide and these compounds—Antineoplastic Alkylating Agents and Primary Amides—highlight a broader class of molecules that share structural or functional characteristics. The evidence suggests that Temozolomide may interact with Cyp3a4 through a mechanism that involves the same enzyme as other alkylating agents, potentially through a shared metabolic pathway or direct binding. The integration of these paths implies that Temozolomide's interaction with Cyp3a4 is mediated by the enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
